## Intent

Correct operator-facing setup documentation made factually wrong by PR 118, documentation only with no behavior change. Verify claims against current code. In .env.example, state that a non-matching REDIS_PASSWORD fails loudly while REDIS_URL and CELERY_* still override derived values. Remove or correct orphaned brain-worker MinIO credential-file stub instructions in .env.example, docs/DEVELOPER_SETUP.md, and docs/features/infrastructure/areas/local-development.md. Keep the diff limited to documentation and comments. Do not fix stale claims caused by a different reason; report them instead.

## What Changed

Final changed paths and statuses:

```text
M	.env.example
```

## Risk Assessment

✅ Low: Documentation-only correction, fully verified against current source behavior (fail-loud REDIS_PASSWORD mismatch and override semantics); only remaining nit is a stale contradicting header comment.

## Testing

Ran the real lib/env.sh Redis derivation function in 5 operator scenarios confirming the corrected .env.example claims: non-matching REDIS_PASSWORD fails loudly with a clear error and non-zero exit, REDIS_URL and CELERY_* overrides are honored over derived values, and a stale changeme_redis REDIS_URL still passes through (validating the retained WRONGPASS warning). Confirmed orphaned brain-worker MinIO credential-file stubs were removed from .env.example and exist nowhere else; PR 118 had already cleaned the two docs files. Ran the focused existing tests (compose contract + redis verify: 12 passed) and swept docs/README for any other stale claims (none found). Overall: change satisfies all intent criteria.

